'''''Carex arenaria''''', or '''sand sedge''', is a species of [[Perennial plant|perennial]] sedge of the genus ''[[Carex]]'' which is commonly found growing in dunes and other sandy habitats, as the [[Binomial nomenclature|species epithet]] suggests ([[Latin]] {{lang|la|[[:wikt:arenarius|arenarius]]}}, "sandy"). It grows by long [[stolon]]s under the soil surface.

